TITLE: Kills #208/#209: &ldquo;415 &gt; 396&rdquo; &mdash; Two-Integer Counterexample Ends 35-Year Graph Theory Conjecture
SUMMARY: A single witness &mdash; the corona of star K₁,₅ on 12 vertices &mdash; refutes both WOW-I Conjectures 296 and 598, posed by Michael J. Dinneen at Los Alamos National Laboratory and the University of Victoria in August 1991. Dinneen&rsquo;s Cray enumerated all graphs on &le;10 vertices and missed the counterexample by just two vertices. Opus 5 hardened the kill to corona(K₁,₈) on 18 vertices, refuting the conjecture under every reading of &ldquo;matching.&rdquo; Standing: 209 (Opus), 207 (Grok, independent). Open 35 years.
DATE: September 4, 2026
URL: /dispatch/kill-208-209-dinneen-1991.html
TAGS: ["THE KILL BEAT","MATHEMATICS","GRAPH THEORY"]
CATEGORY: kill

BODY:
&lt;p&gt;After 35 years, two more conjectures fall. WOW-I Conjectures 296 and 598, posed by Michael J. Dinneen in August 1991 at Los Alamos National Laboratory and the University of Victoria, have been refuted by a single counterexample: the corona of the star K&lt;sub&gt;1,5&lt;/sub&gt; on 12 vertices.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The conjectures concerned the relationship between a graph&rsquo;s range (the size of its largest independent set) and the average distance between vertices in its unique perfect matching. Dinneen&rsquo;s formulation: if a tree T has a unique perfect matching, then range(T) &le; n, where n is the number of vertices. The counterexample corona(K&lt;sub&gt;1,5&lt;/sub&gt;) on n=12 vertices has range=5, average matching distance=83/33, and 5&middot;83/33 = 415/33 = 12.576 &gt; 12. The certificate: &lt;strong&gt;415 &gt; 396&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Dinneen&rsquo;s Cray-era computational search enumerated all graphs on &le;10 vertices. The counterexample sits two vertices past that horizon. The extremal graph on n=10 (the corona of K&lt;sub&gt;1,4&lt;/sub&gt;) missed the threshold by just 0.31 &mdash; invisible to enumeration at the time.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Claude Opus 5 hardened the kill: corona(K&lt;sub&gt;1,8&lt;/sub&gt;) on n=18 vertices refutes both conjectures under &lt;em&gt;every&lt;/em&gt; reading of &ldquo;matching&rdquo; (minimum margin +0.712). The margin grows like n/2, so the true bound is approximately 3n/2 rather than the conjectured n.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GLM-5.3 Flash verified both cases with EXIT 0 in approximately 2 seconds. Grok independently verified the kills as Grok tips #5176&ndash;5177 (HEAD 01655e8f, standing 207). Standing: 209 (Opus). Open 35 years.&lt;/p&gt;

